Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- Every vector variable ($\text{u}$, $\text{v}$, $\text{w}$, $\text{i}$,
  $\text{j}$, $\text{k}$, $\text{a}$, $\text{b}$, $\text{c}$, $\text{n}$,
  $\text{p}$, $\text{r}$, $\text{s}$, $\text{F}$, and $\text{B}$) had been
  converted to upright, non-bold \text{} instead of boldface, matching the
  same defect already fixed for vol3-2-1-vectors-in-the-plane.tex,
  vol3-2-2-vectors-in-three-dimensions.tex, and
  vol3-2-3-the-dot-product.tex, and unlike every other
  vector-notation exercise file in this repo and OpenStax's own boldface
  vector convention; changed every such occurrence to \mathbf{}. The unit
  symbols $\text{C}$ (coulombs) and $\text{T}$/$\text{N}$ (tesla/newtons)
  were left as \text{}, since those are typeset upright by convention, not
  vectors.
- Sixteen occurrences across the file joined the last item of a
  comma-separated list of vectors or points into the same math span as the
  word "and" via \text{and} plus manual \, spacing (e.g.
  "$\text{u},\text{v},\text{and}\,\text{w}$", "$O,A,B,\,\text{and}\,C$"),
  the pattern this skill flags against (English glued into math mode
  instead of plain-text "and" between separate math spans); split each into
  separate math spans joined by plain-text "and" (e.g. "$\mathbf{u}$,
  $\mathbf{v}$, and $\mathbf{w}$", "$O$, $A$, $B$, and $C$"). One of these
  ("the velocity vector v is given by") also left the vector variable v as
  bare, non-mathematical prose; wrapped it in math mode as $\mathbf{v}$.
- "($\text{F}$ in $\text{N})$." trapped a sentence-level closing
  parenthesis inside the math span for the unit N, matching the skill's
  flagged pattern of sentence punctuation trapped inside math; moved the
  closing parenthesis outside the math span, to "$\text{N}$)."
- The wrench figure description for the torque item split "in." and "lb"
  across a stray capital "I" and a stray space ("12 I n.", "10 l b."), a
  conversion artifact inconsistent with the identical units spelled out
  correctly elsewhere in the very same item and its sibling item; corrected
  to "12 in." and "10 lb."
- The determinant displays used the plain-bars notation
  $|\begin{matrix}...\end{matrix}|$ instead of the dedicated LaTeX
  environment for a determinant; changed them all to
  \begin{vmatrix}...\end{vmatrix}.

